Open the keymap FIFO before the uinput settle delay

keymap writes block until fkgpiod has the FIFO open. fkgpiod opened it
only after init_uinput()'s sleep(1), so Instant Play's "keymap resume"
held up a resumed game by about 0.55 s at boot (StarFling Phase 1.2).

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -221,14 +221,13 @@
         openlog("fkgpiod", LOG_PERROR | LOG_PID | LOG_NDELAY, LOG_DAEMON);
     }
 
-    /* Initialize the uinput device */
-    init_uinput();
-
-    /* Initialize the GPIO mapping */
+    /* Initialize the GPIO mapping first: it opens the command FIFO, and
+     * until the FIFO has a reader, every "keymap" write blocks. Instant
+     * Play's "keymap resume" runs during boot, so opening the FIFO only
+     * after init_uinput()'s 1 s settle delay held up a resumed game by
+     * about 0.55 s. Commands written meanwhile wait in the FIFO and are
+     * handled once the main loop starts. */
     if (init_gpio_mapping(config_file, &mapping_list) == false) {
-
-        /* Close the uinput device */
-        close_uinput();
 	if (daemon) {
 
 	    /* Close the syslog */
@@ -236,6 +235,10 @@
 	}
         exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
     }
+
+    /* Initialize the uinput device */
+    init_uinput();
+
     while (true) {
 
         /* Main loop to handle the GPIOs */
